name fly_transect
describe A long straight flight at speed across the region. THIS IS THE STUTTER REPRODUCTION: run_svo asks for a whole-world rebuild once the camera leaves lod_radius*0.5 = 2 metres of the last build centre, and a boosted fly covers that in ~12 ms against a 0.6-1.3 s build -- so builds run back to back for the whole traverse. The frame-time percentiles and the slow-frame-by-cause counts here are the numbers Prompt 004 has to move.
backend both

# 6 s at the un-boosted fly speed (40 m/s) covers 240 m, from x=-120 to x=+120 -- across the
# whole 128 m island rather than 1,920 m out into open sea, which is where a 12 s BOOSTED flight
# ended and why its `final` capture was a featureless dune. The rebuild storm does not need the
# extra distance: run_svo asks for a whole-world rebuild every 2 m of camera motion, so 240 m is
# already 120 requested rebuilds against a 0.6-1.3 s build.
pose_ground -120,0 -90 -6 40
hold forward 6
hold none 1

# A settle before the final capture. A moving scenario requests a whole-world rebuild every 2 m
# (run_svo's lod_radius*0.5), and whether the last one has LANDED by the final frame depends on
# wall-clock timing -- measured: fly_orbit's vk `final` differed from its own golden by 70.4% of
# pixels on a re-run while d3d12's was bit-identical, purely because one run's rebuild arrived
# and the other's did not. That is the rebuild storm Prompt 004 exists to remove; until it is
# removed, a golden taken immediately after motion is not reproducible. Waiting is the honest
# workaround, and this line should be deletable once 004 lands.
wait 3


# GOLDEN POLICY (measured, this scenario has none / only the early ones):
# A capture taken after sustained MOTION is not reproducible on this engine today. Two identical
# runs of the same scenario differ by 5.3% to 35.5% of pixels, because at speed the body outruns the
# LOD rebuild and which tree is resident when it stops decides what it sees. Captures taken AT REST
# reproduce to 0.0001-0.11%, well under the 1.5% gate. So the moving captures here are written for
# eyeballing and deliberately have no golden until Prompt 004 removes the rebuild storm.

capture frame 60 early no-golden
capture frame 400 mid no-golden
capture end final no-golden
assert frames > 0
assert contrast_percent > 6
assert inside_solid == 0

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ goal 273: the regression gate
# A PERCENTILE of the GPU timestamp range across this fixed camera path, per research section 6.8 --
# never a mean (one hitch moves it) and above all never fps, which this machine's 165 Hz
# FIFO_RELAXED panel caps at 155-159 and which therefore cannot express a regression at all.
#
# PER BACKEND, because vk and d3d12 differ by 30-35% here and `ctest -L scenario` runs vk ONLY. A
# single threshold would have to be set by the slower backend, leaving the faster one 35% of slack
# -- a 30% vk regression would sail straight through the gate that CI actually runs.
#
# Each number is ~1.2x the worst of three runs on THAT backend: the smallest margin that survives
# run-to-run noise and still fails when the budget is tightened by 20%, which is goal 273's own
# Check and is demonstrated in the log.
#   vk    ~1592 frames, p95 3.93 3.95 3.88 (1.8% spread)
#   d3d12             p95 4.86 4.86 4.89 4.97 (2% spread)
assert gpu_ms_p95 < 4.5 vk
assert gpu_ms_p95 < 5.7 d3d12
